@node Introduction
@unnumbered Introduction

@command{starter-configurable-service-extras} packages small helpers used
with @command{starter-configurable-service} (@acronym{STCS}).

Today this package ships @emph{process} programs: short-lived commands that
print a single @acronym{JSON} object on standard output. @acronym{STCS}
invokes them through the @code{process-transport} plugin and maps fields
with @code{json-reader}.

A @file{plugins/} tree is reserved for future out-of-tree @acronym{STCS}
shared modules. None are included in version @value{VERSION}.

For @acronym{STCS} itself, see the
@cite{STARTER Configurable Service} documentation in the
@command{starter-configurable-service} package.

@node Processes
@chapter Processes

Both programs are installed under @file{$prefix/bin} (typically
@file{/usr/local/bin}).

@menu
* current-time::
* sun-position::
@end menu

@node current-time
@section @command{current-time}

Prints the local wall clock as @acronym{JSON} (no command-line options).

Example:

@example
$ current-time
@{"year": 2026, "month": 10, "day": 13, "hour": 14, "minute": 30,
 "second": 0, "dayMinutes": 870, "daySeconds": 52200,
 "unix": 1791893400, "UTCOffset": 7200000000, "timezone": "CEST"@}
@end example

Fields include calendar components, minutes/seconds since local midnight,
Unix time, UTC offset (as returned by GLib), and a timezone abbreviation.

Typical @acronym{STCS} use: @code{<command>/usr/local/bin/current-time</command>}
inside a @code{process-transport} with @code{json-reader} maps onto time
inputs (site overlay @file{current-time.xml}).

@node sun-position
@section @command{sun-position}

Estimates solar azimuth and elevation for a given latitude/longitude at
the current local time (converted to @acronym{UTC} for the calculation).

Mandatory options:

@table @option
@item --latitude=@var{LAT} / @option{-a} @var{LAT}
Reference latitude in degrees.
@item --longitude=@var{LON} / @option{-o} @var{LON}
Reference longitude in degrees.
@end table

Example:

@example
$ sun-position --latitude 45.223 --longitude 11.999
@{"timestamp": 1791893400, "latitude": 45.223000, "longitude": 11.999000,
 "azimuth": 204.360031, "elevation": 46.287419@}
@end example

@itemize @bullet
@item @code{azimuth} — degrees from north (0° = north, 180° = south).
@item @code{elevation} — degrees above the horizon.
@end itemize

Typical @acronym{STCS} use: site overlay @file{sun-position.xml} with
@code{process-transport} polling on a cron expression and binding
@code{SUN:azimuth} / @code{SUN:elevation}.

@node Building and Installing
@chapter Building and Installing

Prerequisites: Autotools, pkg-config, GLib 2.44 or newer,
@command{starter-configurable-service} (pkg-config module
@code{starter-configurable-service}), and @command{makeinfo}.

@example
$ ./autogen.sh
$ ./configure --prefix=/usr/local
$ make
$ sudo make install
@end example

Install also ships @file{starter-configurable-service-extras.pc} so other
packages can detect this one with pkg-config.

Build the Info manual:

@example
$ make -C doc info
@end example

@node Plugins
@chapter Plugins

Directory @file{plugins/} is a placeholder for future out-of-tree
@acronym{STCS} plugins (shared objects installed under
@file{$libdir/starter/configurable-service/plugins}). Version
@value{VERSION} does not ship any plugin modules.

